# Web architecture

Reference layout: `app/page.tsx` (RSC) → `app/components/PantryDemo` (client) → `store/usePantryStore.ts` → `@smart-pantry/ui`.

## Decision tree

**New route or page:** `app/<route>/page.tsx` (Server Component by default). Layouts stay in `app/**/layout.tsx`.

**New UI:**
- Reusable across screens / Storybook → `@smart-pantry/ui` (skill: `ui-component-with-storybook`)
- Used only in this app, composed from shared UI → `app/components/<Name>/`
- Do not copy Button-like primitives into `web`

**App component file layout (folders for every island):**
- One folder per component under `app/components/` so the directory never mixes loose files and folders:
  - `ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx`
  - `ComponentName/ComponentName.test.tsx` (when present)
  - `ComponentName/ComponentName.constants.ts` (named constant maps/lists/styles)
  - `ComponentName/index.ts` re-exporting the public API
- Import siblings via `@/app/components/OtherName` (through `index.ts`), not deep file paths.
- Leave a one-off literal inline when it is not a reusable named block. Shared domain values still belong in `lib/`.

**New client state:** Zustand store in `store/use<Name>Store.ts`. Select slices (see `PantryDemo`). Never put Zustand in `packages/ui`.

**New React hook:** reusable across pages → `hooks/use<Name>.ts` (create the folder when needed). Tied to one component → keep it colocated in that component folder.

**Pure logic (no React):** `lib/<domain>.ts` (create when needed). Do not grow `page.tsx` with parsers or validators.

**HTTP / server data:** prefer Server Components, Route Handlers, or `lib/` (including Supabase clients). Never fetch from `@smart-pantry/ui`. Do not add React Query/SWR unless the feature needs client cache.

## What NOT to do

- Do not mark a page `"use client"` only to use a store — extract a client island.
- Do not create Context providers for data that belongs in Zustand.
- Do not fetch or import Next.js APIs from `packages/ui`.
- Do not put feature screens under `packages/ui`.
- Do not leave new component files loose under `app/components/` — always create a folder + `index.ts`.
- Do not grow `ComponentName.tsx` with large constant tables — move them to `ComponentName.constants.ts`.
